Marker file shipped by @DISTRIBUTION@'s base-files to signal that
directories under /usr/local should use 755 permissions owned by
group root, instead of the historical 2775 owned by group staff.

The marker is the file's existence; packages that care check for it.
The prose is documentation only.

Removing this file restores the historical 2775 / group staff
behaviour for /usr/local — discouraged but supported for operators
who have explicit reasons to need it.
